exercises.solution:
```python
def arrangements(items):
    if not items:
        return [[]]
    result = []
    for i in range(len(items)):
        first = items[i]
        rest = items[:i] + items[i + 1:]
        for r in arrangements(rest):
            result.append([first] + r)
    return result
```

This is the proof of Theorem 4 as a program: $n$ choices for the first item, each followed by all $(n - 1)!$ arrangements of the rest, giving $n \times (n-1)! = n!$. (The Lean file builds arrangements the other way round, inserting the first item into every position; both give $n!$.)
